@lang en
-- Tests of ie-words-and-meaning.l4: s 18 lead-in, s 18(a), (c), (j), (i) with the 1971 offset as an input, s 19 and s 20(2).
-- Expected values were decided from the text of each provision (quoted in the comments) and never from the code.
-- Every limb is tested on both sides, and each rule has a case outside it whose answer is an explicit refusal or an explicit FALSE.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-general`
IMPORT `ie-words-and-meaning`

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where a contrary intention appears`
`contrary intention` a b c MEANS
    `Where a contrary intention appears` WITH `in this Act` IS a, `in the enactment itself` IS b, `in the Act under which it is made` IS c

GIVEN d IS A DATE, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A moment in UTC`
`moment` d m MEANS
    `A moment in UTC` WITH `its day` IS d, `its minute of the day` IS m

§ `Section 18, lead-in: "The following provisions apply to the construction of an enactment" (subject to s 4(1))`

#ASSERT     `the section 18 rules apply to the construction of the enactment` (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT     `the section 18 rules apply to the construction of the enactment` (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `the section 18 rules apply to the construction of the enactment` (`contrary intention` TRUE  FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the section 18 rules apply to the construction of the enactment` (`contrary intention` FALSE TRUE  NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the section 18 rules apply to the construction of the enactment` (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE))

§ `Section 18(a): "A word importing the singular shall be read as also importing the plural, and a word importing the plural shall be read as also importing the singular"`

-- a word importing the singular is read as importing the singular and the plural
#ASSERT count (`the numbers a word is read as importing` (JUST singular)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT elem singular (`the numbers a word is read as importing` (JUST singular))
#ASSERT elem plural   (`the numbers a word is read as importing` (JUST singular))
-- and the other way round
#ASSERT count (`the numbers a word is read as importing` (JUST plural)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT elem singular (`the numbers a word is read as importing` (JUST plural))
#ASSERT elem plural   (`the numbers a word is read as importing` (JUST plural))
#ASSERT     `a word importing` (JUST singular) `is read as also importing` plural
#ASSERT     `a word importing` (JUST singular) `is read as also importing` singular
#ASSERT     `a word importing` (JUST plural)   `is read as also importing` singular
#ASSERT     `a word importing` (JUST plural)   `is read as also importing` plural
-- a word importing neither number is outside the section: it is read as importing neither
#ASSERT count (`the numbers a word is read as importing` NOTHING) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT `a word importing` NOTHING `is read as also importing` singular
#ASSERT NOT `a word importing` NOTHING `is read as also importing` plural

§ `Section 18(c): "'Person' shall be read as importing a body corporate (whether a corporation aggregate or a corporation sole) and an unincorporated body of persons, as well as an individual"`

#ASSERT `the word person is read as importing` individual
#ASSERT `the word person is read as importing` `a corporation aggregate`
#ASSERT `the word person is read as importing` `a corporation sole`
#ASSERT `the word person is read as importing` `an unincorporated body of persons`
-- F42: the section lists the kinds; a party of another kind is not answered
#ASSERT REFUSED `the word person is read as importing` `a party of another kind` BECAUSE "section 18(c) names the kinds of party that person imports, so a party of another kind is not answered"

-- "the subsequent use of any pronoun in place of a further use of 'person' shall be read accordingly"
#ASSERT     `a pronoun used in place of person is read as importing` individual `, the pronoun being used in place of a further use of person` TRUE
#ASSERT     `a pronoun used in place of person is read as importing` `a corporation sole` `, the pronoun being used in place of a further use of person` TRUE
#ASSERT     `a pronoun used in place of person is read as importing` `an unincorporated body of persons` `, the pronoun being used in place of a further use of person` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a pronoun used in place of person is read as importing` individual `, the pronoun being used in place of a further use of person` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a pronoun used in place of person is read as importing` `a corporation aggregate` `, the pronoun being used in place of a further use of person` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `a pronoun used in place of person is read as importing` `a party of another kind` `, the pronoun being used in place of a further use of person` TRUE BECAUSE "section 18(c) names the kinds of party that person imports, so a party of another kind is not answered"
-- a pronoun not used in place of 'person' is outside the limb, so the question about another kind of party does not arise
#ASSERT NOT `a pronoun used in place of person is read as importing` `a party of another kind` `, the pronoun being used in place of a further use of person` FALSE

§ `Section 18(j): "A reference to a person in relation to an offence (whether punishable on indictment or on summary conviction) shall be read as including a reference to a body corporate"`

-- arguments: the kind of party; how the offence is punishable; whether the reference is to a person in relation to an offence
#ASSERT     `section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` `a corporation aggregate` `, the offence being punishable` `on indictment`        `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` `a corporation aggregate` `, the offence being punishable` `on summary conviction` `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` `a corporation sole`      `, the offence being punishable` `on indictment`        `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` `a corporation sole`      `, the offence being punishable` `on summary conviction` `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` TRUE
-- not a reference to a person in relation to an offence
#ASSERT NOT `section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` `a corporation aggregate` `, the offence being punishable` `on indictment`        `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` FALSE
-- paragraph (j) adds a body corporate and nothing else; the other kinds of party are the business of paragraph (c)
#ASSERT NOT `section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` individual                      `, the offence being punishable` `on indictment`        `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` `an unincorporated body of persons` `, the offence being punishable` `on summary conviction` `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` `a party of another kind`        `, the offence being punishable` `on indictment`        `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` TRUE
-- F46: the parenthesis names two ways of punishing; an offence punishable in another way is not answered
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` `a corporation aggregate` `, the offence being punishable` `in another way` `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` TRUE BECAUSE "section 18(j) names offences punishable on indictment or on summary conviction, and says nothing of an offence punishable in another way"
-- the first condition is tested first, so a reference that is not to a person in relation to an offence is FALSE, not a refusal
#ASSERT NOT `section 18(j) reads the reference as including a body corporate` `a corporation aggregate` `, the offence being punishable` `in another way` `, the reference being to a person in relation to an offence` FALSE

§ `Section 18(i): "that time shall be determined by reference to the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971" (the offset of that standard time is an input)`

-- Hand-worked from the definition of the input: local time = UTC + offset, so UTC = local time - offset; minutes count from the start of the UTC day.
-- 15:00 on 10 March 2026, offset 0: 900 minutes into 10 March
#ASSERT `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 15 0 0 EQUALS `moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 900
-- 15:00 with the standard time one hour ahead of UTC: 14:00 UTC, 840 minutes
#ASSERT `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 15 0 60 EQUALS `moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 840
-- 15:00 with the standard time five hours behind UTC: 20:00 UTC, 1200 minutes
#ASSERT `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 15 0 (0 MINUS 300) EQUALS `moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 1200
-- hour 0 with the standard time one hour ahead of UTC: 23:00 UTC on the day before
#ASSERT `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 0 0 60 EQUALS `moment` (YMD 2026 3 9) 1380
-- hour 0 and hour 23 are the boundaries of a specified hour
#ASSERT `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 0 0 0 EQUALS `moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 0
#ASSERT `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 23 0 0 EQUALS `moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 1380
-- "a time after a specified hour": 90 minutes after 23:00 is 00:30 the next day
#ASSERT `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 23 90 0 EQUALS `moment` (YMD 2026 3 11) 30
-- "a time before a specified hour": 120 minutes before 03:00 is 01:00; before 01:00 is 23:00 the day before
#ASSERT `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 3 (0 MINUS 120) 0 EQUALS `moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 60
#ASSERT `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 1 (0 MINUS 120) 0 EQUALS `moment` (YMD 2026 3 9) 1380
-- an hour that is not a whole number from 0 to 23 is outside the provision
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 24 0 0 BECAUSE "section 18(i) speaks of a specified hour, so an hour that is not a whole number from 0 to 23 is not answered"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) (0 MINUS 1) 0 0 BECAUSE "section 18(i) speaks of a specified hour, so an hour that is not a whole number from 0 to 23 is not answered"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment in UTC of a time expressed by reference to a specified hour` (YMD 2026 3 10) 1.5 0 0 BECAUSE "section 18(i) speaks of a specified hour, so an hour that is not a whole number from 0 to 23 is not answered"
-- the pass-1 function is the answer when no offset is supplied: it refuses
#ASSERT REFUSED `the clock time of a specified hour in an enactment` 15 BECAUSE "the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 is not in the text of this Act and is not encoded"

§ `Section 19: "A word or expression used in a statutory instrument has the same meaning in the statutory instrument as it has in the enactment under which the instrument is made"`

#ASSERT `the meaning in the statutory instrument of a word` (JUST "a person holding under a lease") `, a contrary intention being` (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST "a person holding under a lease"
#ASSERT `the meaning in the statutory instrument of a word` (JUST "a person holding under a lease") `, a contrary intention being` (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST "a person holding under a lease"
-- the enabling enactment gives the word no meaning: the section supplies none
#ASSERT `the meaning in the statutory instrument of a word` NOTHING `, a contrary intention being` (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a contrary intention (s 4(1)) in the instrument itself, in the Act under which it is made, or in this Act: not answered
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning in the statutory instrument of a word` (JUST "a person holding under a lease") `, a contrary intention being` (`contrary intention` FALSE TRUE NOTHING) BECAUSE "section 19 yields to a contrary intention under section 4(1), and the Act does not say what the word means then"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning in the statutory instrument of a word` (JUST "a person holding under a lease") `, a contrary intention being` (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE)) BECAUSE "section 19 yields to a contrary intention under section 4(1), and the Act does not say what the word means then"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning in the statutory instrument of a word` (JUST "a person holding under a lease") `, a contrary intention being` (`contrary intention` TRUE FALSE NOTHING) BECAUSE "section 19 yields to a contrary intention under section 4(1), and the Act does not say what the word means then"

§ `Section 20(2): "other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the word or expression have a corresponding meaning"`

#ASSERT     `section 20(2) gives the form a corresponding meaning` `another part of speech of the word`   `, the enactment defining or interpreting the word` TRUE
#ASSERT     `section 20(2) gives the form a corresponding meaning` `another grammatical form of the word` `, the enactment defining or interpreting the word` TRUE
-- a different word is not a form of the defined word
#ASSERT NOT `section 20(2) gives the form a corresponding meaning` `a different word`                    `, the enactment defining or interpreting the word` TRUE
-- the enactment does not define or otherwise interpret the word: the section does not reach it
#ASSERT NOT `section 20(2) gives the form a corresponding meaning` `another part of speech of the word`   `, the enactment defining or interpreting the word` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 20(2) gives the form a corresponding meaning` `another grammatical form of the word` `, the enactment defining or interpreting the word` FALSE
